# Hybrid BFF

Auth stays server-mediated. Domain data does **not** get a Server Action
per resource. The browser never sees FastAPI's origin or the token.

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| Session (OTP, Google, refresh, logout) | Server Actions or `app/api/auth/*`. Blocklisted on `/api/backend`. |
| RSC reads | `lib/load-*.ts` → OpenAPI → FastAPI. One hop. Not `"use server"`. |
| Client mutations / live UI | `backendFetch(path)` → `/api/backend/...`. Cookie stays HttpOnly. |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — wrapper action for a GET, or exposing the API host
"use server";
export async function fetchItems() { /* ... */ }
fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL}/items`);

// ✅ GOOD
await loadItems();                    // RSC
await backendFetch("/api/v1/items/"); // client; credentials same-origin
router.refresh();                     // catalog retry — not a BFF GET
```

- Forms that need Zod + `redirect` (e.g. `addItem`) may stay Server Actions.
- Do not add react-query/SWR until a feature needs client cache. Point it
  at `backendFetch`, never at `API_BASE_URL`.
- Do not invent `lib/backend-proxy.ts` or an internal token header. The
  Route Handler reads `accessToken` from the cookie and sets `Authorization`.
- Future live features (solicitudes, chat) follow this table. Delete
  unused wrappers instead of keeping them "for later".
